{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1143964-confused-about-river-hags-in-changeling-20th","id":1143964,"title":"Confused about River Hags in Changeling 20th","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-25T21:30:07-07:00","id":1143964,"title":"Confused about River Hags in Changeling 20th","content":"Hi, I wonder if someone can advise me.<br /> I was quite taken by the description of River Hags in Changeling 20th but I was unsure about a few things. (I'm not really familiar with them from earlier editions which may be a factor. At the same time quite a bit has changed from earlier editions so I'm not sure how relevant that would be.)<br /> Do male river hags exist?<br /> How does River Hag Ugliness work mechanically? (Do River Hags have an Appearance of Zero or a maximum appearance?) <br /> Can River Hags pass as (Ugly) Humans without cantrips? <br /> How do River Hags use Illusions to &quot;dress in the appearance of a beautiful person&quot;? (From what I gathered Metamorphosis One could make them look human but wouldn't make them beautiful and I didn't see anything else to solve this.)<br /> Thanks for any advice anyone can give on this.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mark Storey","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/555-marks4trying","name":"Marks4trying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T23:13:43-07:00","id":1143983,"title":"","content":"Well as far as I can remember they used to be female only, though I could easily misremember this tiny bit, and they were first introduced in KB:Redcaps. They also used to have all redcap birthrights and frailties in addition to their own, breathing underwater and the inability to leave their river, and they had to buy atleast swimming 2 at chargen and had a maximum appearance of 1. These are just from the top of my head.<br /> <br /> As for the illusion my first instinct is to say Chicanery is your art but on a quick glance it now has only the first level as dealing with such trickery, the workings of which in this case are by ST judgement, but at least it should be achivable by Unleashing Chicanery. Metamorphosis could also work, though in that case the change isn't exactly illusory but again it might require Unleashing depending on your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T02:59:09-07:00","id":1144011,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I'm not sure if some of that hasn't changed but it gives me somewhere to start from.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mark Storey","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/555-marks4trying","name":"Marks4trying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:44:15-07:00","id":1144062,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain that C20 does not mention the limit on appearance, though their ugliness is still part of the fluff, nor does it put requirements on abilities at chargen. Also it drops Bully Browbeat from their birthright and replaces it with the waterbreathing, instead of them having three birthrights, and it drops Bad Attitude replacing it with their inability to leave their home river. So basically they are now more in line with general Kith builds.<br /> <br /> So I would personally use C20 writeup but add the appearance limit so that they are more inline with the fluff.<br /> <br /> As for the question of could they pass as ugly humans, of course since like all Changelings they are Fae souls in human bodies. Meaning that only the enchanted and the creatures of the Dreaming see them as they truly are. For the rest they look like ugly, and likely wet, humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T10:15:22-07:00","id":1144111,"title":"","content":"Thanks. That seems very workable. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mark Storey","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/555-marks4trying","name":"Marks4trying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Da